by Phi Phi 211@mtu.edu 
> 3) Guardian Nagas (see #1)

Don't you mean Golden Nagas?

Gremlins are pretty high on my list these days, since the little punks
can be deadly if they swipe a critical intrinsic at a bad time (like,
say, fire resistance).  Plus, they can really multiply quick in the
presence of water, increasing your chances of getting some important
intrinsic swiped (nothing more obnoxious than getting intrinsic teleport
control stolen).  Gelataneous cubes used to be way up there, but they no
longer paralyze you for nearly as long so I don't both with them
nowadays.  Rust monsters are still a pain in the butt.  Pretty much, I
try to get a blessed scroll of genocide, wipe out all "L"s, get
gremlins, golden nagas, rust monsters and then all "n"s in that order,
and I'm happy.  Then I just start wiping out the toughest monsters and
slowly work my way down (if I have enough genocide scrolls and/or magic
markers handy).

